data.content:
## What Changed

Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0 upgrades the underlying library from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1** to **v2**, which aligns with OpenAPI v3.1. Key breaking changes affecting your code:

| Area | v1 (.NET 9) | v2 (.NET 10) |
|------|-------------|--------------|
| Examples | `IOpenApiAny` / `OpenApiString` | `JsonNode` |
| Nullable | `schema.Nullable = true` | `schema.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| Security refs | `OpenApiSecurityScheme` with `Reference` as dict key | String-keyed dictionary |
| Responses | Same API but `OpenApiResponse.Description` is no longer required in the model |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;        // replaces Microsoft.OpenApi.Any
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // Example is now JsonNode, not IOpenApiAny
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    // SecurityRequirement is now Dictionary<string, IList<string>>
    // Use the scheme ID string directly as the key
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { ["oauth2"] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable bool is gone; remove "null" from the type flags instead
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of fixes

1. **`OpenApiString` → `JsonValue.Create(...)`** — the `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace no longer exists.
2. **`schema.Nullable = false`** → **`schema.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null`** — nullability is now a flag in the `Type` enum (OpenAPI 3.1 style).
3. **`OpenApiSecurityScheme` as dictionary key** → **string key `"oauth2"`** — `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is now `Dictionary<string, IList<string>>`.
